<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HUMAN GOLD RUSH LESSON</p><h1>Stories of Trust in Motion</h1><p class="intro">The complete story includes promises, attempts, completions, surprises, disputes, gratitude, and walk-aways.</p><blockquote>What becomes possible when communities remember more than the highlight reel?</blockquote></header><section class="content-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>A five-part story</h2><p>Describe the need, invitation, voluntary responses, fulfillment outcome, and lesson.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>Consent before identity</h2><p>Ask permission before identifying or recording another person. Always offer an anonymous contribution path.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>Remember unseen work</h2><p>Ask whose voice is missing, who performed invisible labor, and which walk-away improved the plan.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h2>Community memory</h2><p>Stories complement the event dataset. They do not replace validated records or justify claims the data cannot support.</p></div></article></section><section class="media-section"><div class="section-heading"><p>MEDIA FOR THIS LESSON</p><h2>Watch, listen, and discuss</h2></div><div class="media-grid"><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 1</small></div><h3>Stories of Trust in Motion: orientation</h3><p>Reserved for the featured story or introductory video.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 2</small></div><h3>Community conversation</h3><p>Reserved for a demonstration, conversation, or local example.</p><a href="#">Discussion guide coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card podcast"><div class="media-frame"><span>◉</span><small>PODCAST</small></div><h3>Listen and reflect</h3><p>Reserved for the facilitator or community podcast episode.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article></div></section>